meridian oss
============

build:  make
run:    make run          (rebuilds meridian.db from data/)
check:  make check        (billing rule checks, bin/billing-test)
reg:    make register     (invoice register for 2026-07)
demo:   make demo         (invoice-api :8082 + dashboard pages on :8083)

binaries land in bin/

  mediation      nightly ingest, writes meridian.db
  inventory-api  :8081   /sites  /circuits  /capacity
  billing-run    monthly invoice register, --json for the reconciliation feed
  billing-test   billing rule checks
  rules-vectors  writes the shared conformance vectors on stdout
  libtelcorules.so  the shared rule library, what vantage loads with ctypes
  invoice-api    :8082   /invoices?acct=...&period=...
  ipam           management address report (10.20.0.0/16)

dashboard/index.html and dashboard/billing.html are static pages, open them in
a browser with inventory-api and invoice-api running.

dashboard/capacity.html is the sales desk capacity check. it asks
/capacity?requested=<mbps> and shows what is left at each customer location.
available = total - allocated, we do not hold back a maintenance buffer.
serviceable locations come from data/locations.csv.

data/ holds the telemetry drops. billing/accounts/ is the account master.

billing rules all live in billing/rules/telco_rules.c. that file is the only
implementation of them anywhere, meridian and vantage both run it:

  R-RATE      whole gigabytes, partial gigs round up, $10 a gig over plan
  R-PRORATE   30 day billing month, mid cycle plan changes split on it
  R-PROMO     promo credits expire at the end of the cycle they were issued
  R-SUSPEND   a suspended line is billed the full month, no credit
  R-LINES     3-9 lines 5% off recurring, 10+ lines 10%
  R-LATEFEE   10 day grace after the due date, then 1.5% of the balance
  R-TAXBASE   GST/HST on the pre discount amount, PST/QST on what is paid
  R-LOYALTY   loyalty credit off the subtotal, applied after tax
  R-ROUND     each charge line rounded to cents, the total is their sum

billing/invoice.cpp marshals an account into the library and copies the result
back out, it does not decide anything. billing/rules/RULES.md has the rule by
rule history, including the three questions that are flagged as undecided.

make vectors writes billing/rules/conformance/vectors.json from the library.
that file is what consumers that cannot link the object are held to (today the
vantage java report module). make check fails if it is stale.

the provinces we bill are BC, AB, ON and QC. the province is on the account
record (PROVINCE=) and on the invoice register page.

vantage-telco vendors billing/rules/ and calls the compiled object through
ctypes, so both registers rate the same. tools/parity in that repo runs them
side by side off the same usage feed and has to come out clean.

contacts: ops-eng (pager), billing questions -> finance
